{"author":"John Wesley","book":"Notes on the Bible","chapter":793,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:wesley:Ps.56","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"John Wesley","authorshipDateRange":"18th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Methodist","translator":null,"edition":"CCEL edition; source omits 2 Samuel 24","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"wesley","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"}},"originalBook":"Psalms","sourceVolumeId":"wesley","source":{"id":"wesley","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"},"title":"Psalms 56","reference":"Psalms 56","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"David complains of his enemies, and begs for mercy, and help against them, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":2,"text":"1-7.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":3,"text":"Expresses his confidence in God, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":4,"text":"8-13.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":5,"text":"To the chief musician upon Jonath-elem-rechokim, Michtam of David, when the Philistines took him in Gath.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":6,"text":"Title of the psalm.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":7,"text":"Jonath-elem-rechokim.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":8,"text":"Which is supposed to be the name of a song.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":9,"text":"4.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":10,"text":"Will praise - I will praise the Lord for his word, for his promises of protection and deliverance, made to his people.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":11,"text":"Flesh - Infirm and mortal men, called flesh by way of contempt, as chap. lxxviii, 39 Isaiah xxxi, 3.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":12,"text":"6.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":13,"text":"They gather - After they have severally employed their thoughts against me, they meet together to compare them, and to put them in execution.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":14,"text":"Hide - They lurk secretly, that they may pry into my most private actions.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":15,"text":"Steps - That they may find some occasion to reproach me.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":16,"text":"Soul - Or, life, to take it away.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":17,"text":"7.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":18,"text":"Escape - Shall they secure themselves by injurious and malicious practices.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":19,"text":"The people - These who are mine enemies.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":20,"text":"8.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":21,"text":"Wanderings - How I have been hunted from place to place.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":22,"text":"Put - Regard and pity them.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":23,"text":"Are they not - But why do I pray to God to do that which he hath already done?","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":24,"text":"12.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":12,"scriptureVerseEnd":12},{"verse":25,"text":"Thy vows - I had made vows to express my gratitude, and resolve to perform them.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":12,"scriptureVerseEnd":12},{"verse":26,"text":"13.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":13,"scriptureVerseEnd":13},{"verse":27,"text":"Walk - That I may serve and glorify thee.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":13,"scriptureVerseEnd":13},{"verse":28,"text":"The light - ln this life.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":13,"scriptureVerseEnd":13}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"Psalms","chapter":56}}